# makepkg build output. Two of these are traps rather than mere noise:
# `src/` and the `symmetria-ide*/` clone are copies of THIS repo (makepkg builds
# from the committed tree), so tracking them embeds a git repository inside
# itself.
#
# The glob is load-bearing: makepkg names that clone after the source URL's
# basename, so it is `symmetria-ide/` from the dev worktree and
# `symmetria-ide-stable/` from the stable one. The bare name matched only dev,
# so a promotion — the one time this package is built from stable — left an
# untracked clone of the whole repo sitting in the stable tree.
src/
pkg/
build/
symmetria-ide*/
*.pkg.tar.zst
